From 78cd4e6dd4cd4ba380496b3467e6b1becc582cb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yetone <yetoneful@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:53:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sessions: a call through magpie in Cindy is counted once,
 as the gateway's (jealousy03888)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

jealousy03888 on Discord: "cindy里用Zcode订阅 同一个请求两个记录是特性吗".
Their Routing list had one ZCode GLM-5.3 request twice: the gateway's row
(ZCode · api.z.ai, 135/37/84,736 tokens, ~$0.026) and five seconds later
a "local session" row on the provider "magpie-beedee1a" with the same
tokens and cost, so Usage and the Requests totals counted it twice too.

Cause: Cindy's import parser gives a custom provider the link's id plus
eight hex digits of a new UUID (`${id.slice(0,24)}-${randomUUID()
.slice(0,8)}`, read in Cindy 0.1.94's app.asar), so magpie's link (id
"magpie") becomes "magpie-<8 hex>", and Cindy's Pi writes that id on
every reply. The Pi reader left out only "magpie"/"dial", so Cindy's
calls through magpie were read as Cindy's own beside the gateway's.

Now piGateway(agent, provider) also takes "magpie-" + eight lowercase
hex digits as magpie's entry, in Cindy's files only (Pi's own and omp's
providers are named by the user; magpie writes "magpie" there). A
provider the user adds by hand in Cindy under the name Magpie gets the
slug "magpie" or "magpie-2", never this shape. callParseVersions raises
cindy to 1, so Cindy's call shards written before are read again once
on update and the duplicates already shown go away (usage's request and
heat caches key on CallCacheVersion, so they are rebuilt too); no other
agent's shards are re-read.

Every other agent's reader was checked for the same gap (an id the app
chooses rather than magpie): OpenCode and ZCode ("magpie", written by
magpie), dsh (magpie's three route names), MiniMax Code
(custom_provider:magpie), Kimi ("magpie/" model prefix), WorkBuddy and
CodeBuddy (models.json vendor magpie), Grok Build (its config.toml
tables), Pi, omp and Raft (models.json "magpie"), Claude Code, Codex
and Antigravity (paired with the gateway's rows by session, response id
or tokens and time). Cindy is the only one whose provider id is made by
the app; Lody and AionUi also import a link but their sessions aren't
read.

TestCindyGatewayCallsCountedOnce puts a Cindy Pi session shaped like
the report (provider magpie-beedee1a, zcode/GLM-5.3, 135/37/84,736,
durationMs 5292) and a reply on a user's own "magpie-relay" into
Cindy's session folder; the first must not be a call, the second must
be one. TestCallParseVersionRaiseReadsThatAgentAlone now restores the
real versions after it.

Run (on mote): gofmt -l internal/sessions (nothing); go vet;
GOOS=linux go vet -tags nogui ./...; GOOS=windows go vet ./...; go build
./... all ok. go test -tags nogui -timeout 45m ./... at 40a287b21+this:
86 packages ok, internal/cli red on two filed reds outside this change:
TestEveryRouteHasACommandOrIsNamed (GET /api/context/reply, #5026,
red alone too) and TestLibraryMCPHub (#4140, passes alone). Rebased on
c3593dc49 (no sessions or usage change between) and run again at the
pushed head: internal/sessions ok, internal/usage ok.

Broken by hand: piGateway's Cindy branch replaced by `return false`:
TestCindyGatewayCallsCountedOnce FAIL ("a call through magpie's link in
Cindy counted as Cindy's own: ... Upstream:magpie-beedee1a ...").

Not tried: a real Cindy session through magpie (none on this machine;
the shape is from Cindy's source and the reporter's screenshot); the
Sessions overview's session count for Cindy, which counts sessions,
not calls, and was not changed.
